# The directory holding your timelines. Each one is a folder in here, named for its id:
#
#   <timelines root>/<timeline id>/data.v1.json
#   <timelines root>/<timeline id>/images/
#   <timelines root>/<timeline id>/narratives/
#
# The data file, the pictures and the prose for a timeline all live in that one folder, so
# copying the folder copies the timeline entire. There is deliberately no separate setting for
# where the images or the narratives go: a second configured path could only ever point
# somewhere that breaks that.
#
# The folder name IS the timeline's identity, and the timelineId inside data.v1.json has to
# agree with it. That is what keeps a folder copied under a new name from quietly serving as a
# second timeline.
#
# This is the source of truth (see docs/data-store.md), not a derived artifact — nothing
# regenerates it, so nothing will silently overwrite your edits:
# TIMELINES_ROOT_PATH='/path/to/timelines'
#
# Or, to run against the fabricated sample data, use the copy in the build output. The
# build refreshes it every time, so writes never dirty the checked-in file:
# TIMELINES_ROOT_PATH='./bin/Debug/net10.0/test/timelines'
#
# Note: .env is loaded with overwriteExistingVars: false, so a value already set in your shell
# WINS over this file. That is what makes `TIMELINES_ROOT_PATH=/tmp/scratch dotnet run …` a safe
# way to point a run at throwaway data without touching this file.
#
# An unset value, or a directory that does not exist, fails at startup with an explicit message
# rather than quietly serving an empty table of contents. An *empty* directory is fine — that
# is a first run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Thumbnails (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where generated thumbnails are cached. They are derived and disposable, and are kept out of
# the timeline folders on purpose: two sizes of every picture in there would make the folder a
# manual chore, and the two would drift the first time a photo was replaced.
#
# Safe to delete at any time; it is rebuilt on demand. Defaults to
# <local application data>/pictura-vita/thumbnails.
# IMAGE_CACHE_PATH='/path/to/cache'


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A note on the two side folders
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Images: the store holds only a file name, and the bytes live in the timeline's images/
# folder. A missing folder is not an error — images are optional, and an episode whose image is
# absent draws exactly like one that never had an image. Put originals in there and nothing
# else. Supported extensions are .jpg .jpeg .png .webp .gif — HEIC straight off an iPhone has
# to be converted first, as the decoder cannot read it.
#
# Narratives: the long-form Markdown account of an episode, in the timeline's narratives/
# folder, again by name only. Only .md is served. Files written by the app are named after the
# episode's title ("moving-to-kalamazoo.md"); files you drop in by hand work just as well, and
# can be picked from the list in the episode dialog.
